{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/hdmuseum/posts/milwaukee-is-the-proud-birthplace-of-harley-davidson-and-we-love-celebrating-our/1031198685707400/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/hdmuseum/posts/milwaukee-is-the-proud-birthplace-of-harley-davidson-and-we-love-celebrating-our/1031198685707400/","title":"Harley-Davidson Museum","description":"Milwaukee is the proud birthplace of Harley-Davidson, and we love celebrating our hometown! Can you guess the iconic Milwaukee location featured in this photo?","language":"en","text":"Milwaukee is the proud birthplace of Harley-Davidson, and we love celebrating our hometown! Can you guess the iconic Milwaukee location featured in this photo?\n\nAll reactions:\n\n23 comments\n\n25 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nTheresa Lin\n\nOriental theater?\n\n4\n\nHarley-Davidson Museum replied\n\n1 Reply\n\nNich Sweet\n\nThe Pfister hotel?\n\n1\n\nFuch Yuh\n\nWish had that 1982 Heritage, just missed one for sale a couple of years ago.\n\nMike Willey\n\nThat is the AMF version! I have a set of NON AMF TANKS for this model produced after the buyback in June of 1981!!! Pristine condition!\n\nDebbie Darlin\n\nOK. So where is it?\n\nCharlie Lecach\n\nI don't know where this 1981 Heritage Edition FLH was photographed, but if you ever do a sexy photo shoot with the 1936 EL, it should be done inside the Schroeder Hotel's Crystal Ballroom (Now called Hilton City Center). After all, that's where it was launched!\n\n2\n\nView all 10 replies\n\nTed Gehrke\n\nVilla Terace\n\n1\n\nMost relevant is selected, so some comments may have been filtered out.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2426.1330459994497,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}